{
  "title": "US airports ground stop explained",
  "lang": "en",
  "engine": "chatterbox",
  "voice": "default",
  "sources": [
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_FAA_ground_stop",
    "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/14/faa-ground-stop-disrupts-nba-nhl-and-college-football-weekend-travel",
    "https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/13/us/live-news/flights-ground-stop-faa"
  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "American airports were collapsing yesterday. But why?",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/ohare.jpg",
            "tag": "Chicago O'Hare · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: Dllu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "kicker": "BREAKING",
            "headline": "All US flights stopped"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Friday afternoon, the FAA stopped every plane from taking off in the United States.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/taxiway.jpg",
            "tag": "Planes waiting · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: 4300streetcar · CC BY 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The FAA controls all air traffic in America.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/artcc.jpg",
            "tag": "FAA air traffic control",
            "credit": "Photo: FAA · public domain"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This only happened two times before: on September 11, 2001, and in January 2023.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "timeline",
          "params": {
            "title": "US-wide ground stops",
            "items": [
              {
                "time": "Sept 11, 2001",
                "text": "Terror attacks"
              },
              {
                "time": "Jan 2023",
                "text": "FAA computer failure"
              },
              {
                "time": "Nov 13, 2026",
                "text": "Network outage"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "So what went wrong? It was not the weather.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/tower.jpg",
            "tag": "Air traffic control tower",
            "credit": "Photo: Harrison Keely · CC BY 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "kicker": "WHY?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The communication network that links air traffic control centers broke down.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "list",
          "params": {
            "title": "What broke",
            "items": [
              "Control centers lost contact",
              "Radio problems",
              "Planes could not leave"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Officials say new equipment sent too much data, and the old system could not handle it. There was no sign of an attack.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "compare",
          "params": {
            "before": "Old system",
            "after": "Too much data from new equipment → overload"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The stop lasted four hours and twenty one minutes.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "timeline",
          "params": {
            "title": "Friday, Nov 13 (Eastern time)",
            "items": [
              {
                "time": "3:54 PM",
                "text": "All departures stopped"
              },
              {
                "time": "8:15 PM",
                "text": "Flights start again"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "More than 4,700 flights were cancelled, and more than 10,000 were delayed.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "bars",
          "params": {
            "title": "Friday flights",
            "bars": [
              {
                "label": "Cancelled",
                "value": 4700
              },
              {
                "label": "Delayed",
                "value": 10000
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "About 1.5 million passengers were affected, and hundreds of planes landed at other airports.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/security.jpg",
            "tag": "Passengers waiting · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: APK · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Flights from Europe and Mexico to the United States were stopped too.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/lax.jpg",
            "tag": "Los Angeles · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: Charles from Port Chester, New York · CC BY 2.0 · Wikimedia Commons"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said it will take some time to fix.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/duffy.jpg",
            "tag": "Sean Duffy · US Transportation Secretary",
            "credit": "Photo: US DOT · public domain",
            "headline": "“It will take us some time”"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Saturday, more than 2,000 more flights were cancelled.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/gate.jpg",
            "tag": "Saturday · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: Beyond My Ken · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "kicker": "STILL DELAYED"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Now leaders want 50 billion dollars from Congress to build a new system.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/airports/capitol.jpg",
            "tag": "US Congress",
            "credit": "Photo: Noclip · public domain",
            "headline": "$50 billion to fix air traffic control"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Will it be fixed before Thanksgiving? Follow for more news.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "title",
          "params": {
            "kicker": "NEXT",
            "text": "Fixed before Thanksgiving?"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}